## The IVG

The Internationale Vereinigung für Germanistik (IVG), or International Association for Germanic Studies, was born in Rome in 1955 to bring together people who study the German language and literature on every continent. Since then it has organized 15 international congresses, one every five years, each in a different country.

The IVG covers research in German linguistics and literature, the teaching of German, German as a foreign language and Yiddish studies. It has no fixed seat: it moves to the country of whoever leads it.

In July 2025, at the general assembly of the Graz congress in Austria, the IVG elected a Latin American president for the first time: the Brazilian Germanist Paulo Astor Soethe, of the Federal University of Paraná. As a result, the next edition of the congress will be held in Rio de Janeiro in 2030.

## IVG Brasil

IVG Brasil is the civil association created by Brazilian Germanists to carry out the IVG's activities in the country during the Brazilian presidency, and in particular to organize the Rio 2030 Congress.

Besides supporting the goals of the worldwide IVG, IVG Brasil works to:

- strengthen Germanic Studies at Brazilian universities, the field known here as Letras Alemão;
- give public visibility to the field's research and output;
- show high school students that studying German opens paths as a researcher, teacher, translator, publicist or cultural agent;
- promote the teaching of German, especially in public schools;
- bring German teachers in basic education closer to the scientific community, through projects and training linked to universities.

## Governance

IVG Brasil is led by the president of the IVG, who is civilly and financially responsible for it. The other bodies advise and oversee.

- **Presidency:** Paulo Astor Soethe (UFPR).
- **Deliberative Committee**, which is also the Organizing Committee of the Rio 2030 Congress: Thiago Viti Mariano (UFPR), Juliana Pasquarelli Perez (USP) and Giovanna Lorena Ribeiro Chaves (UFF).
- **Executive management and treasury:** Luísa de Quadros Coquemala.
- **Fiscal Council:** Zaira França (UFBA), Adriana Fernandes Barbosa (UnB), Mergenfel Andromergena Vaz Ferreira (UFRJ) and Gerson Neumann (UFRGS).

## Network

IVG Brasil works alongside associations of Germanists and German teachers in Brazil and around the world.

- **Germanic Studies:** [ALEG](https://www.aleglatam.org/), [Deutscher Germanistenverband](https://deutscher-germanistenverband.de/), [German Studies Association](https://www.thegsa.org/), [Österreichische Gesellschaft für Germanistik](http://www.oegg.org/)
- **German teaching:** [BraDLV](https://bradlv.com.br/pt/index.php), [IDV](https://idvnetz.org/), [Goethe-Institut Brasil](https://www.goethe.de/ins/br/pt/), [DAAD Brasil](https://www.daad.org.br/)
- **Neighboring fields:** [ABRALIC](https://abralic.org.br/), [ABRAPT](https://abrapt.org.br/)
